// Task 5194 fixture — a minimal `: Rigid` body whose mass-property cells
// (mass / centroid / moment_of_inertia / moi_principal) are auto-derived from
// `geometry` + `material.density` by the stdlib `Rigid : Physical` traits
// (crates/reify-compiler/stdlib/structural_physical.ri).
//
// Used by the GUI-panel surfacing tests (gui/src-tauri/src/tests/engine_tests.rs)
// and the OCCT-free compute-contract regression lock
// (crates/reify-eval/tests/rigid_mass_props_autoderive_gui_path.rs).
//
// The geometry is a SINGLE `box(...)` primitive so it realizes to a
// deterministic `GeometryHandleId(1)` under `MockGeometryKernel` (no OCCT, no
// booleans, no handle non-determinism). The scalar `depth : Length` param
// drives one box dimension so a warm `edit_param` / `set_parameter` round-trip
// can perturb a geometry dimension and re-exercise the surfacing path.
//
// Modelled on examples/structural_traits_dimensioned.ri (RigidPost) and
// crates/reify-eval/tests/rigid_moment_of_inertia_autoderive_smoke.rs
// (AUTO_MOI_POST_SRC).
structure def RigidMassSmoke : Rigid {
    param depth : Length = 300mm
    param geometry : Solid = box(100mm, 100mm, depth)
    param material : Material = Material(name: "steel", density: 7850kg/m^3, youngs_modulus: 200GPa)
    constraint depth > 0mm
}
